For an event $A in cal(F)$ and $X = bb(1)(A)$,
$
  EE[X] & = sum_(omega in Omega) bb(1)(omega in A) dot PP({omega}) \
        & = sum_(omega in A) PP({omega}) \
        & = PP(A).
$
The expectation of an indicator is the probability of the underlying event; this bridge is what lets indicator arguments translate between probabilities and expectations.
